Package: daddyR
Title: Discover Stochastic Differential Equations from Time Series Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Vishwesha", "Guttal", email = "guttal@iisc.ac.in", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Arshed", "Nabeel", role = "aut"),
    person("Ashwin", "Karichannavar", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates data-driven stochastic differential equations (SDEs)
    from scalar and vector time series, following the drift-diffusion
    (Kramers-Moyal) decomposition described in Nabeel, Karichannavar,
    Palathingal, Jhawar, Bruckner, Danny Raj & Guttal (2025)
    "Discovering stochastic dynamical equations from ecological time series
    data", The American Naturalist, 205: E100-E117
    <doi:10.1086/734083>. This is an R port of the 'PyDaddy' Python package
    (<https://github.com/tee-lab/PyDaddy>), reimplemented natively in R with
    a number of correctness fixes and API simplifications documented in
    'DESIGN_DECISIONS.md'.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
